# Sovereign Three.js Backgrounds

Whenever a user requests a "cool background," an "animated background," or specifically asks for the "Sovereign Network" or "Core Brain" visuals, you MUST use the custom `react-three-fiber` components located in our project (e.g., `client/src/components/ThreeBackground.tsx`).

Do NOT use Vanta.js. Do NOT use static CSS gradients as a replacement for 3D elements.

## Available Components:

### 1. `<NetworkScene />`
Use this for hero sections, landing pages, and pitch decks to represent the distributed AI Business Router architecture.
* **Visuals:** Floating spherical nodes connected by lines, volumetric fog, city environment lighting.
* **Usage:** Place it absolutely behind the content.
    ```tsx
    import { NetworkScene } from '@/components/ThreeBackground';
    
    <div className="relative min-h-screen">
       <NetworkScene />
       <div className="relative z-10">...content...</div>
    </div>
    ```

### 2. `<CoreScene />`
Use this to represent the "Kernel," "Baseband," or "MCP Engine."
* **Visuals:** A slowly rotating, wireframe Icosahedron inside a glowing solid Icosahedron, surrounded by stars.
* **Usage:** Place it behind specific technical components or feature cards.
    ```tsx
    import { CoreScene } from '@/components/ThreeBackground';
    
    <div className="relative h-[400px]">
       <CoreScene />
       <div className="relative z-10">...content...</div>
    </div>
    ```

## Implementation Rules:
* Always ensure the canvas container has `absolute inset-0 z-0` (or similar) so it sits behind the actual UI content.
* Ensure the foreground content has `relative z-10` to remain clickable.
* Ensure `@react-three/fiber`, `@react-three/drei`, and `three` are installed.
